# the argument of aquinas-third-way.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# Aquinas, Third Way. Read propositionally; quantifiers over beings are folded into atoms.
# Note: S3 says each possible thing at some time is not; S4 infers that at one time nothing was.
# This step (each at some time -> all at one time) is written as an unstated assumption A1.
# The word "possible" in S4 ("could have been nothing") is not given a separate atom; it is read as "at one time nothing existed".
atom	generated	things in nature are found to be generated and to corrupt
atom	contingent_exist	there are things in nature possible to be and not to be
atom	contingent_sometime_not	that which is possible not to be at some time is not
atom	all_contingent	everything is possible not to be
atom	once_nothing	at one time there was nothing in existence
atom	once_nothing_2	there could have been a time when nothing existed
atom	begin_needs_existing	that which does not exist only begins to exist by something already existing
atom	nothing_now	even now nothing would be in existence
atom	necessary_exists	there exists something the existence of which is necessary
atom	all_necessity_caused	every necessary thing has its necessity caused by another
atom	regress	there is an infinite series of necessary things having their necessity caused by another
atom	self_necessary	there exists some being having of itself its own necessity, not receiving it from another
atom	god	God exists (the being all men speak of as God)
P1	S2	generated	kind empirical
P2	S2	generated → contingent_exist
P3	S3	contingent_sometime_not
A1	-	contingent_sometime_not → (all_contingent → once_nothing_2)
C1	S4	all_contingent → once_nothing_2	from P3 A1
P4	S5	begin_needs_existing
P5	S5	begin_needs_existing → (once_nothing → nothing_now)
P6	S6	¬nothing_now	kind empirical
C2	S7	¬all_contingent	from C1 P4 P5 P6
# "not all beings are merely possible" is taken to mean that something is necessary
A2	-	¬all_contingent → necessary_exists
C3	S7	necessary_exists	from C2 A2
P7	S8	necessary_exists → all_necessity_caused ∨ self_necessary
P8	S9	¬regress
A3	-	all_necessity_caused → regress
C4	S10	self_necessary	from C3 P7 P8 A3
P9	S11	self_necessary → god	kind conceptual
C	S11	god	from C4 P9
